  "source_text": {
    "prototype_id": "A01",
    "title": "Frost at leaf level on the low plain, night Wed 18 → Thu 19 Nov",
    "body": "Clear, calm nights Tue-Thu. Cold air drains off Geraneia and pools on the plain: 2 m air min 0.5 °C at Μεσαίο Χωράφι, 0.0 °C at Κάτω Κάμπος, 0.2 °C at Νότιος Κάμπος. Leaf surfaces can be 2-3 °C colder than the air. Young coriander and dill (Μεσαίο Χωράφι) are the most exposed. Geraneia Slope is warmer (4.0 °C, above the cold layer) and Pachi (5.0 °C, sea).",
    "action": "Wed 18 Nov before sunset: cover coriander + dill (Μεσαίο Χωράφι) with 17-19 g/m² fleece (gains ~1-2 °C). Remove Thu 19 after ~10:00 when thawed, before the windy front on Fri. Thu 19: no harvest of spinach (Κάτω Κάμπος) or chicory before leaves thaw (~10:00).",
    "why_rule": "Warn when forecast 2 m min <= 2 °C AND night wind <= 5 km/h AND clear sky on parcels below 50 m. Leaf surface can be 2-3 °C below air on such nights. Damage temperature for each crop is NOT set by the app – your agronomist can set it.",
    "severity": "high"
  },
  "notes": "Expected follows RULES.md + QA P1-3/P1-4, not the prototype: every affected parcel (P1, P2, P5) and every night that meets the rule (16→17, 17→18, 18→19), not only Wed→Thu. Confidence Low because no parcel is calibrated (RULES FROST); the prototype said Medium. Endive PL15 (P5, ready) gets the thaw guard."
